00:28:54.220 --> 00:29:02.760
Samuel Smith: who has a token that allows them to access the control API that authorizes something to be signed.

220
00:29:02.760 --> 00:29:22.219
Samuel Smith: So, a side-channel attack on entitlement signing infrastructure is not necessarily an attack on the hardened cryptographic algorithms going on in the secure hardware. It simply can be an attack out here at the edge on the authorization token granted to any signing requester.

221
00:29:22.430 --> 00:29:33.559
Samuel Smith: And so, the full spectrum of, of, of edge attacks apply to your… as a side-channel attack to your signing infrastructure.

222
00:29:33.640 --> 00:29:50.650
Samuel Smith: So even though you're following best practice here, if you're not following best practices here, then you're vulnerable to side-channel attack. Things will get signed, and if you're using bearer tokens out here, you won't even know they got signed, because there's no way to track

