00:43:55.420 --> 00:44:10.789
Samuel Smith: then you can't use it for most of the use cases of verifiable credentials. That DID method is in… is violating best practices for key management. It is foundationally and fundamentally insecure as a DID method, because you can't use it for those purposes.

